    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d973">

                <pb facs="0955" n="697" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg697"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-01-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>889. Your 1400, January 4. As message appears to be partially in code, the
                    Department would be pleased to forward it after being put <pb facs="0956"
                        n="698" xml:id="pg698"/> in plain, commercial language. Bring this to early
                    attention of Sir Edward Grey to have
                    little delay as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
